WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:02.389
LSD stands for lysergic acid

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:03.969
diethylamide, a chemical derived

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:04.949
from fungus.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.269
This is not the psychedelic that

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:07.319
they're thinking about or that

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:08.549
they're having fun with.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:09.869
The kind of power washes you from

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:10.409
the inside.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.819
Something that does approximate a

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.039
natural religious experience.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.949
You're colonizing it, they're

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:17.369
damaging us. You're embracing our

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:18.029
cultures.

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:20.159
A gruesome spectacle of how drugs

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.223
can ruin a brilliant mind.

00:00:21.224 --> 00:00:22.892
That does Iive a life of pleasure

00:00:22.893 --> 00:00:23.998
and joy.

00:00:23.999 --> 00:00:24.959
There are a lot of people out there

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.519
who just want to explore their own

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.709
consciousness, want to have mystical

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:30.449
experiences, and we feel like they

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:31.450
should be able to do that.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.169
Everywhere around us, there are

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.569
signs of a psychedelic renaissance

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.519
in medicine, therapy,

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.889
commerce and the arts.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:45.419
These drugs are getting serious,

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.309
positive coverage in glossy

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.349
magazines, best selling books,

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.539
literary memoirs, documentaries

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:53.099
and hit podcasts.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.809
I wanted to know what this was like,

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:57.059
and so I arranged a series

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:58.919
of guided

00:00:58.920 --> 00:00:59.609
trips.

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:01.529
Ayahuasca is usually described

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:02.530
as a grandmother spirit and

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.699
I met

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:06.509
her.

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:08.039
Performers like Reggie Watts,

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:09.929
Melissa Etheridge and the members

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:11.549
of The Flaming Lips openly

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:12.689
acknowledged the role of

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:15.089
hallucinogens in their work.

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:16.019
I was 16.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:17.999
I experienced LSD for the first

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.309
time. So much came into perspective.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:22.139
I think the discussion

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:23.969
of psychedelics

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:26.399
and plant medicine

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.079
is extremely important.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.059
And a flourishing psychedelic comedy

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:31.949
scene is springing up all over

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:32.909
the place.

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:34.889
Ketamine is like if someone

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:36.389
just like, threw you out of an

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:39.209
airplane but gave you a tranquilizer

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:40.210
for.

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:44.729
I guess I'm toppling around through

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:47.045
the atmosphere.

00:01:47.046 --> 00:01:48.959
Nearly every country

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:50.879
in the world, including the United

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.799
States, is a signatory

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.989
to an international law banning

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:57.119
the use, sale, cultivation

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.459
and possession of dangerous drugs

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.319
that have no useful place in

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.489
medicine.

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:03.689
But federal prohibition of

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.519
psychedelics, a term that refers

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.589
to a broad category of consciousness

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:09.839
and perception altering substances,

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:11.729
is also changing.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.349
The Food and Drug Administration is

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.479
expected to approve therapy using

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.399
psilocybin, the psychoactive

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.229
ingredient in magic mushrooms

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:21.119
and MDMA, the drug

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.649
also known as Ecstasy.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:23.669
And Molly.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:25.619
Oregon and Colorado, have already

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.569
decriminalized the recreational

00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:30.149
use of plant based psychedelics.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.009
Word is that even the president,

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:33.959
famous as a teetotaler for

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:35.939
having an addict son and

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:37.349
as a major force behind the

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:39.239
half-century long drug war

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:41.309
is very open minded about

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:44.039
medicinal use of psychedelics.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:46.229
The most recent pulsing Day-Glo

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:47.669
sign that the psychedelic

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:49.409
renaissance is here took place in

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:51.119
Denver in late June at the

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.039
Psychedelic Science 2023

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:54.989
conference, organized and hosted

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:57.329
by the Multidisciplinary Association

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:59.369
for Psychedelic Studies or

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:00.089
MAPS.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:02.099
This is about humans helping humans.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:05.039
Founded in the late eighties, MAPS

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.169
has spent decades working to get FDA

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:09.119
approval for MDMA- assisted

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.279
therapy for PTSD and related

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:12.479
conditions.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:15.269
At the conference, a reported 13,000

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:17.099
people gathered to talk about

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.259
what seem like every possible topic

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:21.209
related to the productive use of

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:22.709
these substances.

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:24.179
According to MAPS founder Rick

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:26.339
Doblin, this is not the far

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:28.559
out radical reordering of society

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.359
envisioned by Timothy Leary, the

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:32.459
Harvard psychology lecturer turned

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.619
psychedelic evangelist.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:35.789
We look at what happened in the

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:37.679
sixties, and a lot of the

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:39.389
things that came about from the

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:41.249
psychedelics were

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:42.599
frightening to the culture.

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:51.309
Stand still.

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:52.269
Reality. Man.

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:53.529
Reality.

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:55.359
I could see the center of the earth.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.369
In pursuit of mainstream acceptance

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:59.139
and to gain the approval of federal

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:00.639
regulators and establishment

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:01.449
figures.

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:03.639
MAPS is emphasizing the medical

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:05.499
benefits of psychedelics over

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:07.419
their potential to bring spiritual

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:09.189
enlightenment and societal

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:10.659
transformation.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:12.399
Large pharmaceutical companies have

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:14.259
entered the field, putting much

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:16.569
needed capital into research.

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:18.338
But they've also stirred controversy

00:04:18.339 --> 00:04:20.708
by attempting to patent compounds

00:04:20.709 --> 00:04:22.449
that the grass roots say shouldn't

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:24.129
be commercialized because they

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.499
belong to everyone, especially

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:28.329
indigenous communities that use them

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:29.589
first.

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:30.969
But the biggest takeaway from the

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.679
MAPS conference is that there's no

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:34.179
inherent conflict between the

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:35.619
science and spirituality of

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:37.749
psychedelics, and that a former

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:39.759
Republican governor, a current

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:41.589
Democratic governor, religious

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:43.449
seekers, tech-bros and

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:45.849
unapologetic recreational users

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:47.919
can be allies in pursuit of the same

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.059
goal.

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:50.799
This event may be remembered as the

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:52.359
beginning of a new psychedelic

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:54.819
renaissance with immense potential

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:56.889
to radically change therapy,

00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:58.989
medicine, work, art

00:04:58.990 --> 00:04:59.990
and community.

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:10.700
Message. It's very simple.

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:14.220
Six words.

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:16.800
Turn on.

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:18.960
Tune in.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:20.880
Drop out.

